// Address layout for x86_64 user programs and servers.
//
// Programs (musl-linked, also native sysl) load into the high user
// carve-out at VA 0x60000000 (matches aarch64 — same `slix-prog.ld`
// script). Per-process VMA layout (code + stack VMAs) is the single
// source of truth — see `oskit/kernel/vma.lsysl::VMA_DEFAULT_*`.
// Initial-SP / stack-low values are surfaced to PM and RS via
// `svc_vma_default_initial_sp` / `svc_vma_default_stack_low`
// (syscalls 96/97) — no fixed PROG_USP/PROG_SSP constants here.
//
// Servers: code at 0xD4000, 32KB stack. Servers have large BSS
// (RS ~128KB) and need ~176KB to 0x100000. The legacy `[0xCC000,
// 0x100000)` carve-out backing SRV_USP/SRV_SSP is a PHASE 1
// REPLACEMENT TARGET (Phase D of the VMA-list handoff retires it,
// migrating servers to the same 0x60000000 carve-out as programs).
//
// PLATFORM_NAME (below) is the auxv `AT_PLATFORM` value — kept here
// because the prog build can't drag in cpu.lsysl's kernel externs.

module oskit.arch

val SRV_USP  = 0xD4000
val SRV_SSP  = 0xD3000

// AT_PLATFORM string for the SysV initial stack auxv. ld-musl reads
// this via `__init_libc` -> `__libc.platform` and uses it to pick
// HWCAP-gated string routines. Must match what musl was built for —
// we cross-build x86_64-slix-linux-musl, so the platform name is
// the unprefixed arch name.
val PLATFORM_NAME = "x86_64"
